  min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL,
  financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true,
  description = $desc$The University Postgraduate Award (UPA) is the University of Wollongong's own living-allowance stipend for Doctoral and Master of Philosophy candidates, allocated on merit in UOW's main scholarship round and open to both domestic and international students. The stipend is AUD 38,420 per annum at the 2027 rate, non-taxable for full-time candidates and indexed annually, paid for three and a half years full-time for a doctorate or two years for a Master of Philosophy. International applicants apply by the main round's international closing date (23 May) when applying for their degree through UOW Apply Online, and successful candidates commence in the following Autumn session. The UPA is the stipend route available to international candidates at UOW: the parallel Australian Government AGRTP Stipend Scholarship at UOW is, on UOW's own scholarship pages read for this record, restricted to Australian and New Zealand citizens and Australian permanent residents. The UPA covers living costs only; UOW's separate International Postgraduate Tuition Awards (IPTA) under its HDR scholarship policy are not part of this award and are not bundled into this record.$desc$,
  requirements = $req$Be commencing a Doctoral degree or Master of Philosophy at the University of Wollongong (current and future students are listed as eligible student status). UPAs are limited in number and allocated based on merit each year. Apply for the UPA by following the directions in the UOW Apply Online degree application before the relevant closing date - 23 May for international applications, 3 October for domestic applications - and be ready to commence in the Autumn session following application. International candidates must also satisfy student visa requirements. Note the parallel AGRTP stipend at UOW is domestic-only, so international applicants are considered for the UPA instead.$req$,
  funding_type = 'University-funded living stipend (UOW); international tuition awards (IPTA) are a separate scheme',
  tuition_coverage = $tc$The UPA itself is a living-allowance stipend and does not pay tuition. UOW offers separate International Postgraduate Tuition Awards (IPTA) under its HDR scholarship policy, but an IPTA is not part of the UPA listing read for this record, so no tuition benefit is claimed here - international applicants should budget for tuition unless also awarded an IPTA or other fee support.$tc$,
  living_allowance = 38420,
  english_requirements = 'English minima are set by UOW HDR admission and the HDR Scholarship Policy rather than on the UPA listing; no single score is published on the page read, so none is stored.',
  required_documents = $json$["HDR degree application via UOW Apply Online, following the in-application directions to be considered for a UPA","Academic transcripts and evidence of research merit for the competitive main round","English proficiency evidence per UOW HDR admission requirements"]$json$,
  website_url = 'https://www.uow.edu.au/research/graduate-research/scholarships/items/university-postgraduate-award-upa.php',
  source_url = 'https://www.uow.edu.au/research/graduate-research/scholarships/items/university-postgraduate-award-upa.php',
  application_url = 'https://www.uow.edu.au/study/apply/',
  deadline_date = '2027-05-23', deadline_type = 'fixed', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL,
  rounds = $json$[{"round":"Main round (annual) - international applications","closes":"23 May (next: 2027-05-23)","commencement":"Autumn session following application"},{"round":"Main round (annual) - domestic applications","closes":"3 October"}]$json$,
  recurrence = 'annual',
  expected_opening_period = NULL,
  expected_deadline_period = $exp$Annual main round: international applications close 23 May and domestic applications 3 October each year, for commencement in the following Autumn session.$exp$,
  application_status = 'upcoming',
  verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true,
  last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(),
  notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (pass 99) from the University of Wollongong's official University Postgraduate Award (UPA) scholarship listing fetched the same day (the previously stored UOW scholarships URL now returns 404): UPA is UOW-funded, Doctoral/MPhil only, allocated on merit, student type 'Domestic students, International students'; 2027 stipend AUD 38,420 p.a. non-taxable full-time, indexed annually; duration 3.5 years doctoral / 2 years MPhil; closing dates 23 May (international) and 3 October (domestic); apply within the UOW Apply Online degree application; commence the following Autumn session. IMPORTANT: the parallel AGRTP Stipend Scholarship listing at UOW (also fetched) states it is available to Australian citizens, New Zealand citizens or Australian Permanent Residents only (student type: Domestic students), so the UPA - not the AGRTP - is the correct international record for UOW, and the AGRTP's identical AUD 38,420 (2027) figure is not presented as an international offer. An older cached snippet showed a 2026 UPA stipend of AUD 36,943; the live page's 2027 figure is stored. Coverage is Living Stipend only: UOW's International Postgraduate Tuition Awards (IPTA) exist under its HDR Scholarship Policy but are not part of the UPA listing, so no tuition coverage is claimed. deadline_date stores the next published international close (2027-05-23). Previous record was the generic RTP framework at reliability 4 (invented USD 41,000 and copied August 31 deadline already stripped). university_scholarships row 536 synced; source 2675 repointed from the bare domain.$note$,
