-- 442 Flinders -> FIPRS, AUD 36,061 p.a. + international tuition paid
UPDATE scholarships SET
  title = 'Flinders International Postgraduate Research Scholarship (FIPRS)',
  provider = 'Flinders University',
  coverage_type = 'Full Tuition + Stipend',
  amount_usd_value = 0,
  deadline = $dl$Annual international round: the 2027-intake round opened 30 April 2026 and closed Thursday 18 June 2026 (Australian Central Standard Time). Dates for the next round are not yet published on the FIPRS page. Apply for HDR admission first, then for the International RHD Scholarship Group; AGRTPS applicants are automatically considered for FIPRS.$dl$,
  degree_levels = $json$["Master's","PhD"]$json$,
  eligible_majors = $json$["Areas of research concentration at Flinders (fields where the university has particular strength and external funding)"]$json$,
  eligible_countries = $json$["All countries except Australia and New Zealand (Australian permanent residents excluded)"]$json$,
  min_gpa = NULL, min_ielts = NULL,
  financial_need_based = false, merit_based = true,
  description = $desc$The Flinders International Postgraduate Research Scholarship (FIPRS) is Flinders University's own scholarship for international higher-degree-by-research candidates (for visa purposes it is not a Commonwealth Sponsored Scholarship). It pays the international student tuition fees charged by Flinders for the research higher degree and a living-allowance stipend of AUD 36,061 per annum tax free at the 2026 full-time rate, indexed annually and paid fortnightly, tenable for up to three and a half years for a research doctorate. Students moving to Adelaide from overseas can also claim an establishment allowance of up to AUD 1,485 towards relocation costs and airfares against receipts. Only a limited number are awarded each year and the round is highly competitive: applications are scored on academic merit, academic research training and research outputs (up to five publications), and Flinders notes that in 2026 successful applicants submitted five publications, so applicants without publications are unlikely to be competitive. Applicants for the government AGRTPS (International) at Flinders are automatically considered for the FIPRS in the same international round.$desc$,
  requirements = $req$Be a citizen of any overseas country except New Zealand, holding neither Australian citizenship, Australian permanent resident status nor New Zealand citizenship; intend to commence full-time study for a higher degree by research in Australia for the first time in the year of the award (narrow exceptions for recent starters who could not apply in time or who terminated within six months); enrol in an area of research concentration at Flinders; and satisfy all HDR entry requirements including English proficiency, with English evidence lodged with the application (for the round read, test results had to remain valid until 31 March 2027, otherwise the application is ineligible). You must have a Flinders academic's agreement to supervise you, with email evidence included - without a supervisor you will not be considered. Selection is by the Scholarships Committee on academic merit and research potential, scored including up to five publications (each with a coversheet and URL, normally not more than five years old and in English); two academic referee reports must reach Flinders by the closing date. Incomplete applications are not accepted.$req$,
  funding_type = 'University-funded (Flinders) international tuition payment + living stipend; not a Commonwealth Sponsored Scholarship',
  tuition_coverage = 'The FIPRS pays the international student tuition fees charged by Flinders University for the research higher degree for the scholarship tenure (up to 3.5 years for a research doctorate).',
  living_allowance = 36061,
  english_requirements = $eng$Applicants must satisfy Flinders' English Language Proficiency Requirements for HDR Candidature, with evidence provided when the application is lodged; for the round read, English test results had to be valid until 31 March 2027 or the scholarship application was ineligible. No single test score is stated on the FIPRS page itself, so none is stored.$eng$,
  required_documents = $json$["HDR admission application via StudyLink (first), then the International RHD Scholarship Group application via the Flinders Student System","Email evidence of a Flinders academic's agreement to supervise","Up to five publications, each with a completed coversheet including the publication URL","Research proposal of approximately 500 words","Certified copies of all university-level academic transcripts, translated into English","Two academic confidential referee reports returned to Flinders by the closing date","Updated CV with work/research experience and full publication list","English proficiency evidence valid to the date specified for the round"]$json$,
  website_url = 'https://www.flinders.edu.au/scholarships/flinders-university-international-research-scholarship',
  source_url = 'https://www.flinders.edu.au/scholarships/flinders-university-international-research-scholarship',
  application_url = 'https://www.flinders.edu.au/international/apply/apply-research-degree/how-to-apply',
  deadline_date = NULL, deadline_type = 'not_published', deadline_range_start = NULL, deadline_range_end = NULL,
  rounds = $json$[{"round":"International RHD round for 2027 (AGRTPS + FIPRS)","opens":"2026-04-30","closes":"2026-06-18 (Australian Central Standard Time)","status":"closed"}]$json$,
  recurrence = 'annual',
  expected_opening_period = NULL,
  expected_deadline_period = $exp$Annual international round (a limited number of FIPRS each year): the 2027 round ran 30 April-18 June 2026. Dates for the next round had not been published when the page was read on 2026-10-26; expect a similar Autumn (southern hemisphere) window and verify on the FIPRS page.$exp$,
  application_status = 'closed',
  verification_status = 'verified', source_reliability = 10, is_active = true,
  last_verified_at = now(), last_updated_at = now(),
  notes = $note$REWRITTEN 2026-10-26 (pass 99) from Flinders University's official FIPRS scholarship page fetched the same day (overview, benefits, eligibility, selection criteria and application information): university-funded (explicitly not a Commonwealth Sponsored Scholarship for visa purposes); pays international tuition fees plus a stipend of AUD 36,061 p.a. tax free (2026 full-time rate, indexed annually, paid fortnightly) for up to 3.5 years (research doctorate); establishment allowance up to AUD 1,485; open 30 April-18 June 2026 for the 2027 round; citizens of any overseas country except New Zealand (no AU citizenship/PR or NZ citizenship); first-time full-time HDR commencement in Australia; supervisor agreement mandatory; scored on academic merit, research training and up to five publications (2026 successful applicants submitted five). AGRTPS (International) applicants are automatically considered for FIPRS; the separate AGRTPS listing itself was not separately read into this record's values. Previous record was the generic RTP framework at reliability 4 (invented USD 40,000 and copied August 31 deadline already stripped; the stored scholarships-system URL was stale). Next round dates are not published, so deadline_date is NULL/'not_published' with status closed. university_id remains NULL because no Flinders University record exists in the universities table (checked 2026-10-26); adding that university record and linking this scholarship is a separate cataloguing task, as with Adelaide University (id 328). Source 2525 repointed from the bare domain.$note$,
  university_id = NULL,
  award_amount = 36061, award_currency = 'AUD', award_period = 'year', award_basis = 'fixed'
WHERE id = 442;

